{"name":"Tan Temptation","hex":"#f0bd9e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"},{"term":"temptation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of tempting.","The condition of being tempted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temptation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Temptation","blocks":[{"text":"Temptation is a desire to engage in short-term urges for enjoyment that threatens long-term goals. \nIn the context of some religions, temptation is the inclination to sin. Temptation also describes the coaxing or inducing a person into committing such an act, by manipulation or otherwise of curiosity, desire or fear of loss something important to a person."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/William_Blake_Eve_Tempted_by_the_Serpent.jpg/330px-William_Blake_Eve_Tempted_by_the_Serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temptation","wikidata":"Q1053973"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)","wikidata":"Q1670336"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguere